  "body": "## What changed\n\n`assets/posts/haas.cps` now writes these NGC words. The source is the Haas Mill NGC Operator's Manual, 2025 edition (public on haascnc.com). The page numbers are the printed page numbers.\n\n| #1977 item | State | Change and source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `G91` modal at `M30` | fixed | `retractHome()` writes `G90` directly after each `G91 G28` retract: the program end, a setup-change stop, and a trip home. The end is now `G91 G28 Z0` / `G28 X0 Y0` / `G90` / `M30`. Sample program, p. 449; G28, p. 337. |\n| `G53` retract | fixed | `G53 G49 G0 Z<safeRetractZ>`. A home ask (the program end, a trip home) adds `G53 G0 Y0.`. A setup-change stop lifts Z only. \"Completion\" blocks, pp. 202 and 204. The next section's tool call writes `G43 H<n>` again. |\n| Retract choice documented | fixed | `docs/decisions/1977-haas-ngc-words.md`. The default stays `G28` (now with `G90`). `G53` stays an option. |\n| `G94` in the safe-start block | fixed | `G17 G90 G94 G5x G40 G49 G80`. G94, p. 386. |\n| `M4` reverse spindle | fixed | `millSpindleReverse = true`. `PARAM MillSpindle reverse` starts `S.. M4`. The next section starts `M3` again. M03/M04, p. 436. `Haas` is removed from `tool_gate.rs::M3_ONLY_POSTS`, as decision 4031 says. A G84 under M4 is refused by name (G84 is the right-hand tap: pp. 224, 381). |\n| `explains = \"paren\"` + `explain(words)` | already fixed | PR #1814 (#1388), on main. This PR adds `explainWords` for the Haas meaning of G76 (fine bore, p. 371) and of M7, M73/M74, M83/M84, M88/M89. |\n| Coolant-off codes | fixed | M88 -> M89 (p. 449), M83 -> M84 (p. 449), M73 -> M74 (p. 447). M9 stays for M8 and M7 (the NGC shower coolant: M09 stops it, p. 438), and for any other start code. |\n| `G74` left-hand tapping | left | The app refuses a left-hand tap before the post runs (`posting_family.rs`, #1453). The stream has no word for the tap hand. G74 needs a stream word, a manifest flag and app changes. The refusal is safe in the meantime. This item stays open on #1977. |\n\nAlso left: the manual says to write `M88` before the spindle speed (p. 449). The post writes it after `S.. M3`. The control then stops and starts the spindle again. This is slower, not unsafe. It stays open on #1977 too.\n\n## Pinning tests (each fails on `origin/main`'s `haas.cps`)\n\n- `crates/post/tests/setup_change.rs`: `haas_safe_start_block_states_feed_per_minute`, `haas_program_end_restores_absolute_mode_before_m30`, `haas_g53_retract_cancels_the_length_offset_and_brings_y_home`\n- `crates/post/tests/haas_dwell_cycles.rs`: `haas_reverse_mill_spindle_starts_m4_for_its_section_only`, `haas_refuses_a_right_hand_tap_under_a_reverse_spindle`\n- `crates/app/tests/coolant_followups.rs`: `haas_stops_each_coolant_option_with_its_own_off_code`\n- `crates/app/tests/thread_passes.rs`: `a_left_hand_cut_mill_under_m4_climbs_clockwise_and_posts_m4` (Haas now posts M4. The refusal side uses `tormach.cps`.)\n- `crates/app/tests/cutter_hand.rs`: Haas leaves `M3_ONLY`. The M3-only check in `an_edit_to_left_hand_refuses_generation_and_post_until_the_operation_asks` uses Tormach PathPilot.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n33 Haas goldens changed:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/haas/*.nc` (17)\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/inch/haas/*.nc` (2)\n- `inverted/haas_x.nc`, `program_entry/haas_pause_home.nc`, `synth_haas.nc`\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/{bore,explain,fine_bore,ream}/haas.nc`\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/haas/*.nc` (7)\n\nEach golden has the same two edits, and nothing else changed:\n\n1. The safe-start line gets `G94` after `G90` (in each section).\n2. After the program-end `G28 X0 Y0`, a new line `G90` comes before `M30`. In `program_entry/haas_pause_home.nc`, the `G90` was already there (a trip home), so only `G94` changed.\n\nThe explain golden also reads `(XY PLANE, ABSOLUTE POSITIONS, FEED PER MINUTE)` on the safe-start line. \"WORK OFFSET 1\" no longer fits the 60-character comment budget, so the explain helper drops it. The new `G90` line reads `(ABSOLUTE POSITIONS)`.\n\nThe `macro_b` reader of `inverted_probe.rs` now accepts `G94` as a no-op, because it is the only feed mode that the reader reads.\n\n## Readings\n\nOn `origin/main`, the default program end is `G91 G28 Z0` / `G28 X0 Y0` / `M30`, and `G91` is active at `M30`. On this branch it is `G91 G28 Z0` / `G28 X0 Y0` / `G90` / `M30`. In G53 mode it is `G53 G49 G0 Z0.` / `G53 G0 Y0.` / `M30` on the shipped Haas machines (`safeRetractZ` 0).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- This was not run on a real Haas control or on the Haas simulator.\n- M73/M74 and M83/M84 were not tested on a machine that has the Tool Air Blast or Auto Air Gun option. The shipped Haas machine files state only `Flood M8`.\n\n## Gate\n\nLog: `gates/1977-326770b51.log` (first line `326770b515482169e32c717749ab3b3305767188`, the final head).\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 855 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (68.2 min). The plan includes the pinning suites and `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work` (all ok).\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- An earlier head (`12e02c605`) had one red test, `cutter_hand::an_edit_to_left_hand_refuses_generation_and_post_until_the_operation_asks`. It used Haas as an M3-only post. The second commit fixes it.\n\nP3: no heavy step.\n\nChangelog: Haas post: the safe-start block states G94, the program end restores G90 before M30, the G53 retract cancels the tool length offset (G49) and brings Y home, a reverse mill spindle starts M4, and each coolant option stops with its own off code (M89, M84, M74).\n\nProcess change: no\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRefs #1977\n",
